{
  "name": "bark-beetle",
  "_about": "The spruce bark beetle (Ips typographus), 5 mm long: a hairy, dark brown cylinder -- the pronotum a long hood hiding the head from above, rough with small bumps in front; the wing cases ending in a steep, hollow, shiny declivity rimmed with four teeth a side; short elbowed antennae with a round club; short legs. Coat: a young one, light brown. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
